{"id":1847842,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-27T20:16:13.345Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/frAVM0kHSDd999SAZwxZL0ZPae8.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":6000,"genres":[{"id":99,"name":"Documentary"}],"homepage":"","id":1847842,"imdb_id":"tt52456174","origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"ja","original_title":"The Weight We Share","overview":"For centuries, porters known as bokka have transported essential supplies across Japan’s mountainous regions, carrying loads and playing a vital role in supplying remote mountain huts. With the rise of modern transportation, fewer than a dozen full-time bokka remain in Oze National Park. Amongst them is Masato Hagiwara. Having left Oze for Tokyo and spent time abroad, Hagiwara eventually returned home, where he now lives with his wife, Yuyu, and their children. Framed as a personal letter to his children, the documentary explores how Hagiwara balances his personal aspirations with his family responsibilities amidst the uncertain future of his profession.","popularity":0.097,"poster_path":"/kcTLcP97Nmw5L7S8qcoQheLxwUh.jpg","production_companies":[],"production_countries":[],"release_date":"2027-03-26","revenue":0,"runtime":20,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"Japanese","iso_639_1":"ja","name":"日本語"}],"status":"Post Production","tagline":"Masato Hagiwara, one of Japan's few remaining traditional mountain porters, carries supplies across Oze while raising two young children, navigating his identity as a bokka and parent amidst an uncertain future.","title":"The Weight We Share","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":6699921,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Masato Hagiwara","original_name":"Masato Hagiwara","popularity":0,"profile_path":null,"cast_id":1,"character":"Self","credit_id":"6b08856643b31a19d9156a75","order":0},{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":6699922,"known_for_department":"Acting","n